    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S2781A\n\nSPONSOR: STEC\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend chapter 368 of the laws of 2008, amending the tax law\nrelating to authorizing the county of Warren to impose an additional\nmortgage recording tax, in relation to extending the effectiveness ther-\neof\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo extend the state's authorization permitting the county of Warren to\nimpose an additional mortgage tax through Dec. 1, 2025\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 - Authorizes to impose an additional mortgage tax through Dec.\n1, 2025\n\nSection 2 - Provides effective date and date of repeal\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nOn Jan. 20, 2023, the Warren County Board of Supervisors adopted Resol-\nution No. 47 of 2023, which seeks authority for the continuation of its\nadditional mortgage tax.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the state\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall tax effect immediately and be deemed repealed Dec. 1,\n2026\n",
